-- הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 "תשלום קצובת נסיעה", מהדורה 8 (2.3.2023)
-- Edition 8 of the Accountant-General's travel-allowance instruction. Its
-- change table names a footnote to 2.1.5; what the text changes from
-- edition 7 is the blind employee (a full position, or by the hour, 2.3.6),
-- the Sabbath and holiday tariff, now double (2.4.1), and annex B's code
-- 1360, now two single trips a week, there and back. The rest it repeats
-- from edition 7, and takes from that file by import.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT `kitzuvat-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-common`
IMPORT `taarifei-nesia-in-force`
IMPORT `2023-01-26_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v7`

-- Tariffs: the notice's (`travel fares`, read off the notice in force by
-- `the travel allowance on the route` below). No rule here rounds
-- (convention rounding.default).

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: ‘משרה מלאה’ here is
-- the blind employee's basis for the allowance (five times the monthly
-- ticket, 2.3.6), not the hours of work and rest.

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: ‘בעל’ here is the holder of a
-- post or of a service or assigned car (‘בעל רכב צמוד’, ‘בעל נהג צמוד’),
-- not a husband; the instruction sets one travel allowance for every
-- employee, man or woman, and does not distinguish between them.

-- not weighed against `the Advance Notice Law`: ‘חודש סיום העסקה’ here is a
-- month in which the travel allowance is paid pro rata (2.1.5), not notice
-- of dismissal or resignation.

§ `הוראת תכ"ם 13.4.2 תשלום קצובת נסיעה — מהדורה 8`

§§ `1 מבוא`

-- 1.1, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-1
GIVEN `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `edition 8 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit` IF
    `edition 7 applies to` `employed by a government ministry or an auxiliary unit`

-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-2 Further payments in Eilat and the Negev are the notice "תשלומים לנוסעים / עובדים באילת ותוספת ערבה", which the corpus does not hold; no rule here.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3 akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-3/p2 The instruction's purpose; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_1__subpara_1-4 A pointer to annex A, whose definitions the rules below cite; no rule.

§§ `2.1 זכאות לקצובת נסיעה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1 The heading "זכאות לקצובת נסיעה"; its clauses follow.

-- 2.1.1, 2.2.1 and its cases, annex A's definitions 1 and 7, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-1 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-3 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-2__cls_2-2-1__pnt_2-2-1-4 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 8` m IF
    `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 7` m

-- 2.1.2 and annex A's definition 4, as in edition 7: one residence.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_4
`the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 8` MEANS `the residences the allowance is paid from, edition 7`

-- 2.1.3, as in edition 7: a single trip a week from the workplace to the
-- permanent home. Annex B's code 1360 now pays "2 נסיעות בודדות למקום
-- המגורים הקבוע פעם בשבוע (הלוך וחזור)": two single trips, there and back,
-- where the clause refunds one, from the workplace to the home
-- (F-2023-03-02_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v8-b). The reading adopted:
-- the annex's two trips, the edition's own change to the code (edition 7's
-- annex paid one), with the clause's "נסיעה בודדת" read as the single-trip
-- tariff the trips are paid at.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-3
`the trips home a week as 2.1.3 prints it, edition 8` MEANS 1

@ref akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2/t1
`the trips home a week as annex B pays them, edition 8` MEANS 2

`the trips home a week, edition 8` MEANS `the trips home a week as annex B pays them, edition 8`

`2.1.3 and annex B pay a different number of trips home, edition 8` MEANS
    NOT (`the trips home a week as 2.1.3 prints it, edition 8` EQUALS `the trips home a week as annex B pays them, edition 8`)
#ASSERT `2.1.3 and annex B pay a different number of trips home, edition 8`

-- 2.1.4, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-4
`the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 8` MEANS
    `the refund depends on the frequency of transport or the hours of work, edition 7`

-- 2.1.5, its tariffs and annex A's definitions 2-3, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-5__pnt_2-1-5-2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 8` f m IS
    `the monthly employee's allowance, edition 7` f m

-- 2.1.6, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-1__cls_2-1-6
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 8` amount m IS
    `the partial allowance for a partial State-funded month, edition 7` amount m

§§ `2.3 קביעת זכאות לקצובת נסיעה בעקבות רפורמת דרך שווה`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.3.1-2.3.2, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-2
`the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 8` MEANS
    `the train is refunded with every other means of public transport, edition 7`

-- 2.3.3, as in edition 7.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-3
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`, `the equalisation the notice sets` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 8` m `the equalisation the notice sets` IS
    `the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 7` m `the equalisation the notice sets`

-- 2.3.4-2.3.5 and annex A's definition 5, as in edition 7: the hourly
-- employee and the volunteer, the daily tickets for the days travelled, no
-- more than the monthly ticket.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-4/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-5/p2 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance for travel to work, edition 8` f m IS
    `the allowance for travel to work, edition 7` f m

-- 2.3.6 and annex A's definition 6: a blind employee employed in a full
-- position is paid five monthly tickets; one employed by the hour, five
-- times the daily tickets for the days travelled, but no more than five
-- monthly tickets. The entitlement cancels every other in the instruction.
-- A blind employee employed by the month in a part position is in neither
-- sentence, and is paid as any other employee: as the clause is printed.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6/p2 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-6/p3 akn:att_1__hc_1__para_6
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the blind employee's allowance, edition 8` f m IS
    BRANCH IF NOT m's `blind` THEN NOTHING
           IF m's `kind of employee` EQUALS `an employee paid by the hour`
           THEN JUST (min (5 TIMES `the daily passes for the days worked` f m) (5 TIMES f's `monthly free pass`))
           IF m's `in a full position` THEN JUST (5 TIMES f's `monthly free pass`)
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- 2.3.7, as in edition 7: 128 shekels a month in addition.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-3__cls_2-3-7/p2
GIVEN m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 8` m IS
    `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 7` m

§§ `2.4 קצובה בגין נסיעה בשבתות וחגים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4 The heading; its clauses follow.

-- 2.4.1-2.4.2: the daily ticket "חופשי יומי - אוטובוס + רכבת" doubled
-- ("כפול"), for each Sabbath or holiday day the employee actually came; not
-- with a service or personal car, nor in an office with a shuttle.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-1 akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-2
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 8` f m IS
    2 TIMES `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 7` f m

-- 2.4.3: within "the payment cap, as in section 2.3 above", which section
-- 2.3 does not state (F-2023-03-02_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v8-a). The
-- reading adopted: the cap is an input.
@ref akn:hc_1__para_2__subpara_2-4__cls_2-4-3
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER @desc the cap 2.4.3 sends to section 2.3, which states none
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 8` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    min (`the allowance for travel to work, edition 8` f m PLUS `the Sabbath and holiday allowance, edition 8` f m)
        `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`

`the caps section 2.3 states, edition 8` MEANS EMPTY

`section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 8` MEANS
    `the caps section 2.3 states, edition 8` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `section 2.4.3 refers to a cap section 2.3 does not state, edition 8`

`why 2.4.3 gives no figure for the cap, edition 8` MEANS
    `the text is silent` "F-2023-03-02_takam_H-13-4-2_kitzuvat-nesia_v8-a"

-- The month's allowance: none where 2.2 takes the employee out; the blind
-- employee's in place of every other where 2.3.6 gives one; otherwise the
-- allowance with the Sabbath days, within the cap, the locality supplement
-- and the weekly trips home in addition.
GIVEN f IS A `travel fares`, m IS A `travel month`, `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance, edition 8` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    IF NOT `entitled to the travel allowance, edition 8` m THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the blind employee's allowance, edition 8` f m
         WHEN JUST b THEN b
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
                 `the allowance within the payment cap, edition 8` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`
            PLUS `the supplement for a locality without public transport, edition 8` m
            PLUS `the weekly trips to the permanent home` f m `the trips home a week, edition 8`

