§§ `3-4 מסמכים ישימים ונספחים`

-- akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-1 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-2 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-3 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-4 akn:hc_1__para_3__subpara_3-5 The applicable documents (the takshir's chapters 28.3 and 16.6, the form, the two notices); a source list, no rule.
-- akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-1 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-2 akn:hc_1__para_4__subpara_4-3 The list of annexes; no rule.
-- akn:att_1__hc_1/p1 Annex A's title "הגדרות"; its definitions are cited by the rules that use them.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1/p1 Annex B's title; its clauses follow.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_2 The heading of annex B's table of payroll codes; the table's code 1360 is cited where the weekly trips home are counted, its other rows are payroll coding.
-- akn:att_2__hc_1__para_3 The codes of the public-transport lines are the notice's; a pointer, no rule.
-- akn:att_3__hc_1/p1 akn:att_3__hc_1/p2 akn:att_3__hc_1/t1 Annex C, the table of the editions' changes; a record, no rule.

§§ `התעריפים — the notice in force`

-- The edition reads the monthly free pass and the daily free pass, the single fare; here they are read off the notice
-- "לוח תעריפי נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית" in force on the month's day (HOD
-- 13.4.2.1, `taarifei-nesia-in-force`), for the employee's route. Where
-- the notice prints no tariff the edition reads, there is no answer.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE @desc the month's day
      m IS A `travel month`
      `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel allowance on the route, edition 8` r d m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to` IS
    CONSIDER `the travel fares of the route on` r d TRUE TRUE FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST f THEN JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 8` f m `the payment cap 2.4.3 refers to`)

-- The equalisation supplement the notice in force sets, on the route's
-- monthly free pass.
GIVEN r IS A `travel route`, d IS A DATE
      m IS A `travel month`
      x IS A NUMBER @desc the allowance paid before the reform, every component included
      `the highest allowance of 2022` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the travel-allowance equalisation on the route, edition 8` r d m x `the highest allowance of 2022` IS
    CONSIDER `the tariffs of the route on` r d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST rt THEN
        CONSIDER rt's `route monthly pass`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST monthly THEN
            CONSIDER `the equalisation supplement in force on` d x monthly `the highest allowance of 2022`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s THEN JUST (`the travel-allowance equalisation, edition 8` m s)

§§ `Worked examples`

`placeholder fares, edition 8` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 300
        `daily free pass`       IS 20
        `single fare`           IS 15
        `intercity single fare` IS 0

`edition 8 pays` m MEANS `the travel allowance, edition 8` `placeholder fares, edition 8` m 1330

#ASSERT `edition 8 pays` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) EQUALS 300

-- 2.4.1: four Sabbath days at a doubled daily ticket.
`a month with four Sabbaths, edition 8` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 4 FALSE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 8 pays` `a month with four Sabbaths, edition 8` EQUALS 460

-- 2.3.6: a blind hourly employee of 10 days, five times 200; a blind
-- employee in a full position, five monthly tickets.
`a blind hourly employee's month, edition 8` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `an employee paid by the hour` 10) TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 8 pays` `a blind hourly employee's month, edition 8` EQUALS 1000
`a blind full-time employee's month, edition 8` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE 0 0
#ASSERT `edition 8 pays` `a blind full-time employee's month, edition 8` EQUALS 1500

-- 2.1.3 as read: four weeks of two single trips home at 15, in addition.
`a relocated employee's month, edition 8` MEANS
    `the travel month changed` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) TRUE FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE 4 0
#ASSERT `edition 8 pays` `a relocated employee's month, edition 8` EQUALS 420

-- On 1.6.2023, a monthly employee of 22 days on `a 30 km route` (the
-- Tel Aviv codes before the reform, 30 km by bus after it): the edition's
-- allowance on the tariffs the notice in force prints.
#ASSERT `the travel allowance on the route, edition 8` `a 30 km route` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2023) (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330 EQUALS
    JUST (`the travel allowance, edition 8` `the route's fares on 1.6.2023, edition 8` (`an ordinary travel month` `a monthly employee` 22) 1330)

`the route's fares on 1.6.2023, edition 8` MEANS
    `travel fares` WITH
        `monthly free pass`     IS 255
        `daily free pass`       IS 28
        `single fare`           IS 12
        `intercity single fare` IS 0
